**Story & Context:** At 134 BPM, the same three-note pitch cell is played on two different bridge regions. Malik keeps the drum pattern unchanged so Bridge Swap becomes the obvious section change. During the brighter bridge position, hats thin and the santoor SHIMMER is allowed to ring longer. Amina answers with muted minor-seventh Wurlitzer shells. Danish uses daf edge taps in place of the usual club squeak. Midway through, Zoya performs a rapid tremolo burst that Malik refuses to quantize; the machine groove stays fixed while the acoustic shimmer floats above it.

