**Story & Context:** The closer runs at 132 BPM and begins with no electric bass. Zoya plays slow isolated strikes followed by exaggerated hand damping. Malik builds the rhythm from the MUTE points rather than the HIT points, placing kick clusters immediately after silence. Leah uses low chalumeau pedals beneath the open gaps. Amina remains sparse until the final third, then introduces brighter octave Wurlitzer taps. Danish adds daf bass strokes only after every second Damp Drop. The final minute strips the arrangement to santoor, one kick, and room tone. Zoya performs one last full Rebound Chain and mutes the strings completely; the track ends before the expected kick returns.

